Package: uwcc
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 python3-numpy (>= 1.26),
 python3-pil (>= 10),
 python3-pyqt6 (>= 6.6),
 ffmpeg,
Recommends:
 python3-opencv (>= 4.10),
 python3-pyqt6.qtmultimedia,
Description: local underwater video color correction
 Desktop application and command-line tools for underwater video correction,
 with adaptive white balance, temporal smoothing, editable grades, presets,
 batch processing, stabilization, and video export.
 .
 Classical correction works offline without model weights. Neural enhancement
 and denoise require separately prepared models and an optional inference
 runtime. Model weights and GPU runtimes are not included in this package.

Package: uwcc-model-tools
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 uwcc (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3-torch (>= 2.6),
 python3-onnx (>= 1.17),
 python3-onnxruntime (>= 1.21),
 python3-opencv (>= 4.10),
 ca-certificates,
Description: upstream model download and conversion tools for UWCC
 Provides uwcc-models to download pinned upstream weights, verify checksums,
 convert models to ONNX, and prepare optional NVIDIA denoise variants.
 .
 Conversion uses Ubuntu's CPU PyTorch and ONNX packages. Downloads and
 conversion are explicit user operations, never package installation hooks.
 No model weights are redistributed.

Package: uwcc-nvidia
Architecture: amd64
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 uwcc (= ${binary:Version}),
 python3-venv,
 ca-certificates,
Recommends: uwcc-model-tools (= ${binary:Version})
Description: private NVIDIA runtime setup and launcher for UWCC
 Provides uwcc-nvidia-setup to install a pinned ONNX Runtime CUDA wheel and
 its CUDA/cuDNN libraries into a user-owned Python environment, and
 uwcc-nvidia to launch UWCC using that environment.
 .
 Setup requires explicit invocation, network access, and a compatible
 NVIDIA GPU and driver. It validates CUDA inference before enabling launch.
 System Python and GPU drivers are not modified. CUDA libraries and model
 weights are not included in the Debian package.
